   Read SPEC-v2.md before any task. Do one task at a time.
   - Sandbox only. Never hardcode secrets. Never print .env values.
   - Never invent PayPal endpoints or fields. If unsure, stop and ask me.
   - Never run commands that write to ./data/panapay.db. Tests use DB_PATH=:memory:.
   - Money is integer cents. The LLM never does arithmetic, status, or escalation decisions.
   - All model calls go through src/lib/llm.js. Read invoice status only via derive().
   - Read from the customer table, not party, for receivables.
   - No mocked PayPal responses. Webhooks verify signatures and unique event_id.
   - After every change run npm test and show me the real output. Do not say "done" without it.
   - Keep changes small. Tell me every file you touched.